  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nLight showers linger across portions of the area late this\nmorning and will gradually clear from west to east this\nafternoon. Like yesterday, lingering cloud cover will keep\ntemperatures on the cooler side...only topping out in the low\n70s across much of central Nebraska. This is a large departure \nfrom western Kansas where mostly clear skies will allow highs \nto approach 100 degrees in many areas. \n\nThis evening, convection is expected to develop over western\nKansas. Initially, convective parameters would favor a few of\nthese storms becoming strong to severe. These storms should \ngenerally weaken as they move northeastward into our area later \nin the evening hours, but some sub-severe hail cannot be ruled\nout in portions of northern Kansas. Scattered showers and \nthunderstorms persist into Friday morning. In all, some\nlocations could see an additional 1.00-1.50\", but most spots\nlikely will only see 0.25\" or less. These showers are \nanticipated to clear by mid morning, resulting in a drier and \nwarmer afternoon for Friday. \n\nThis warming trend continues into the weekend as upper level \nridging builds over the central CONUS. Temperatures likely reach\nthe 90s across the entire area Saturday, with some locations \napproaching 100 degrees on both Sunday and Monday. Heat index\nvalues near 105 degrees are likely (50% chance) in at least \nsome areas on Saturday, and are a near certainty (80%) on \nSunday/Monday. Some areas (especially the eastern half) could \neven see heat index values exceed 110 degrees on Sunday/Monday \n(40-50% chance). If these trends hold, heat headlines are likely\nto be issued on upcoming shifts. \n\nThe upper ridge weakens with a few disturbances by the middle of\nnext week. As such, temperatures trend a bit cooler with some\nchances for rain. That said, meaningful rain is far from a \nguarantee at this point. Many global ensemble members maintain\ndry or mostly dry conditions for the middle of next week.",
